[00:55.75] Let me walk a while alone
[01:00.85] Among the sacred rocks and stones
[01:06.73] Let me look in vain belief
[01:11.68] Upon the beauty of each leaf.
[01:28.14] There is green in every glade
[01:33.89] The tree tops lean providing shade
[01:39.62] Maypoles spin in happy sound
[01:44.44] All nature's strength around.
[02:01.28] And there's a horse that feels no pain
[02:06.45] Its iron strength to take the strain
[02:12.14] Children rock it to and fro
[02:17.73] And gaily drink its colour glow.
[02:23.19] Ah-ah-ah, ah-ah-ah
[02:28.15] Ah-ah-ah, ah-ah-ah
[02:33.55] Ah-ah-ah, ah-ah-ah
[02:39.27] Ah-ah-ah, ah-ah-ah.
[02:52.62] Above, the sky, devoid of cloud
[02:58.11] Thinks not to cast a thunder shroud
[03:03.91] Upon this place so full of joy
[03:09.24] A field of gold of love's employ.
[03:15.06] Ah-ah-ah, ah-ah-ah
[03:19.82] Ah-ah-ah, ah-ah-ah
[03:25.12] Ah-ah-ah, ah-ah-ah
[03:31.23] Ah-ah-ah, ah-ah-ah.
[04:32.81] So why my heavy heart, you say?
[04:38.17] When tears would stain the sights so gay
[04:44.02] My brother's dreams once here did soar
[04:49.53] Until he died at the hand of needless war.
[05:01.03] Ah-ah-ah, ah-ah-ah
[05:03.98] Ah-ah-ah, ah-ah-ah
[05:12.55] Ooh-ooh-ooh, ooh-ooh-ooh
[05:16.99] Ooh-ooh-ooh, ooh-ooh-ooh.
